==Behavior and Culture==
{{Quote Box|style=float:none; max-width:none|''Dov wahlaan fah rel. We were made to dominate. The will to power is in our blood. You feel it in yourself, do you not? I can be trusted. I know this. But they do not. Onikaan ni ov dovah. It is always wise to mistrust a dovah. I have overcome my nature only through meditation and long study of the Way of the Voice. No day goes by where I am not tempted to return to my inborn nature.''|Paarthurnax{{ref|name=Paarthurnax}}}}
[[File:ON-statue-Dragon Totem.png|right|200px]]
[[File:ON-crown store-Dragon's Treasure Trove.jpg|A Dragon's Treasure Hoard|thumb|left]]
Blessed with remarkable intelligence, Dragons are nonetheless susceptible to feelings of pride and melancholy. Dragons possess an innate urge to dominate others that is near-impossible to overcome. As such, they are distrustful creatures, even of each other. Despite this, they are also somewhat social, and can be driven mad by captivity and isolation.{{ref|name=Paarthurnax}} In the mind of a Dragon, being powerful and being right are the same, thus they make no distinction between speaking and fighting; battles between them are actually deadly verbal debates.{{ref|name=Loading|[[Skyrim:Loading Screens#Dragons|Loading screens]] in ''[[SR:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}{{ref|name=Arngeir}} Dragons are known for their custom of sosmir, the blood allegiance, a mystically binding pact and an unbreakable bond, stronger than any vow uttered by a mortal, which causes the Dragon bound by it to pay their debt by the ancient magic.{{ref|name=Nahfahlaar}}

''[[Lore:Wisdom of the Flying Gods|Wisdom of the Flying Gods]]'' records a worshipper's interpretations of Draconic sayings. These emphasize recognizing one's own strengths and weaknesses, anticipating betrayal while allowing tactical betrayals, attending to surrounding dangers, securing resources, and seeking explanations beyond appearances. Despite this culture of caution, Dragons are also urged to persevere and seek glory when faced with challenges, soar higher to the sky rather than returning to the safety of the ground.{{Ref|name=Wisdom|{{Cite Book|Wisdom of the Flying Gods}}}}

Dragons are known to hunt for food, while they are primarily carnivorous, some have been observed grazing on vegetation. Dragons seem to have a preference for hunting intelligent prey, as they enjoy the extra challenge it provides.{{ref|name=VoD}} Dragons are known to prefer inhabiting mountains.{{ref|name=Paarthurnax}} Some stories tell of a Dragon named Akatosh co-mingling with and organizing groups of Dragons in isolated mountain villages, although this representation may be entirely fictional.{{ref|name=KE}} There is some indication that Dragons are capable of practicing smithing.{{ref|name=FAOT|{{Cite Book|Famed Artifacts of Tamriel}}}}

Dragons are known to collect hoards of treasure.{{ref|[[Online:Dragon's Treasure Trove|Dragon's Treasure Trove]] and [[Online:Ruby Dragon Skull|Ruby Dragon Skull]] item descriptions in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=Dreek}}
{{NewLine}}

==Characteristics==
[[File:ON-render-Lair of Maarselok 02.jpg|Maarselok causing Azure Blight corruption|thumb|right]]
As beings known of their high magical affinity, Dragons are sensitive to and can sense arcane phenomena. They are known to be able to sense the accumulation of magic even across large distances, and can even sense specific characteristics about the source of the magic itself. Traits such as the power belonging to another Dragon and that Dragon's disposition, the age of the one the magic comes from, and even whether they are suffering from some illness, are all things a Dragon's senses can perceive.{{ref|name=Nahfahlaar}} As children of Akatosh, Dragons are especially attuned to the flow of time, and possess the ability to sense events which disrupt or break its flow.{{ref|name=Paarthurnax}}

Dragons possess the ability to devour things beyond the physical, and have been known to eat things such as [[Lore:Souls|souls]], lifeforce, and even the lunar energies of [[Lore:Jode's Core|Jode's Core]] in order to increase their power. This arcane feeding process can sometimes cause the Dragon's size to increase and its very form to change.{{Ref|name=Alduin}}{{ref|name=Nahfahlaar}}{{Ref|name=Odahviing}}{{ref|name=ESOJC}}{{ref|name=Mulaamnir|[[Legends:Mulaamnir|Mulaamnir]]'s dialogue in ''[[Legends:Legends|Legends]]''}} The lifeforce of Dragons themselves can also be channeled into other things, whether willingly or unwillingly, though only specific things which have it in their nature to fully devour Dragons can absorb it fully.{{Ref|name=KatD}}{{ref|name=ESOCadwell|[[Online:Cadwell|Cadwell]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Elsweyr|Elsweyr]]''}}{{ref|name=ESOKhamira|[[Online:Khamira|Khamira]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Elsweyr|Elsweyr]]''}}

A Dragon's presence can have an effect on the conditions of the surrounding area. The long imprisonment of the Dragon Laatvulon within Doomstone Keep caused the fort to become infused with his "icy malice", making frost cover large sections of the structure and the corpses within rise as ice imbued undead, even after his stay there ended. At Sunspire, the Dragon Yolnahkriin resided in the caldera, where his presence is said to have "stoked the sleeping mountain's fire".{{ref|name=Nahfahlaar}}{{ref|name=ESODG|[[ON:The Dragonguard|The Dragonguard]] quest in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Elsweyr|Elsweyr]]''}}{{ref|name=ESOMojha|[[Online:Mojha|Mojha]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Elsweyr|Elsweyr]]''}} 

A Khajiit Moon-Priest's account, transcribed by a scholar of the [[Lore:Mages Guild|Mages Guild]], describes [[Lore:Pridehome|Pridehome]], the Pride of Alkosh, its Clan Mothers, and heroes as ideals existing beyond the world's tapestry and time. These ideals, such as the Doom to Come for which the adepts of Pridehome tried to prepare, have always existed and will always exist. Dragons, the Moon-Priest explained, were the harbingers of the Doom to Come, bringing unbalance to the world on their [[Lore:Return of the Dragons|returning wings]].{{ref|name=Pridehome|{{Cite Book|Pridehome: A Place Outside Time?}}}}

Dragons' wills can be overcome with the [[Lore:Thu'um|thu'um]]. In {{Year|4E 201}}, the Last Dragonborn used it to compel Sahrotaar to carry them to [[Lore:Miraak|Miraak]] in [[Lore:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]]. During the ensuing battle, Miraak consumed the souls of three Dragons in his service to replenish his strength.{{Ref|name=DBSummit|Events of [[Skyrim:At the Summit of Apocrypha|At the Summit of Apocrypha]] in ''[[Skyrim:Dragonborn|Dragonborn]]''}}

==Variants and Mimicry==
[[File:ON-render-Sunspire.jpg|A Red Dragon|thumb|left]][[File:MER-art-Sahrotaar And Miraak.webp|A Serpentine Dragon|thumb|left]]
Dragons' individual appearances can vary wildly, possessing variations in head-shapes, horns, spikes, tails, and other attributes.{{ref|name=ESODragons|[[ESO:Dragon|Dragons]] in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} A Dragon's color is often indicative of how powerful it is,{{ref|name=Loading}} though this is not always the case.{{ref|name=ESODragons}} Brown-skinned Dragons and green-skinned "Blood Dragons" are generally weaker than the white-skinned "Frost Dragons" or bronze-skinned "Elder Dragons" and "Ancient Dragons".{{ref|name=Loading}}{{ref|name=SkyrimDragons|[[Skyrim:Dragon|Dragons]] in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} Dragons of blue, gold, and grey scales are also known to exist.{{ref|name=ESODragons}} 

Two particularly distinct types of Dragon are '''Red Dragons''', some of which are "Fire Dragons", and '''Black Dragons''', some of which are "Storm Dragons".{{ref|name=MA}}{{ref|name=VoD}}{{ref|name=ESODragons}} Originally from Akavir,{{ref|name=MA}}{{ref|name=PGE1Cyro}} these Dragons do not seem to take part in the hierarchies of other Dragons.{{ref|name=VoD|{{Cite Book|Varieties of Dragons: An Initial Exploration}}}} Many Red Dragons throughout history have served with or under mortals.{{ref|name=PGE1Cyro}}{{Ref|name=Odahviing}}{{ref|name=Nahfahlaar}}{{ref|name=DrPaint}}

Serpentine Dragons found on [[Lore:Solstheim|Solstheim]], are named for their distinct, [[Lore:Snake|snake]]-like heads. Revered Dragons have strange flat heads and some are known to have semi-aquatic behavior. The incredibly powerful Legendary Dragons are known to possess strange compound eyes.{{ref|name=SkyrimDragons}} River Dragons were said to reside in Cyrodiil during Tiber's reign; they are known to rust their hides in bodies of water.{{ref|name=PGE1Cyro}}

[[Lore:Jill|Jills]] are mythical beings, said to fix the world during [[Lore:Dragon Break|Dragon Breaks]].{{ref|group=TRL|[[General:A Child's Tamriel Bestiary (French translation)|French translation]] of ''[[Lore:A Child's Tamriel Bestiary|A Child's Tamriel Bestiary]]''}}{{intnote|nb2|[nb 2]}} Some sources describe them as female Dragons.{{ref|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|Nu-Hatta of the Sphinxmoth Inquiry Tree|ns_base=GEN}}}}{{ref|name=NMI|group=UOL|[[General:Nu-Mantia Intercept|Nu-Mantia Intercept]]}} Female Dragons are also mentioned in the historical fiction ''[[Lore:King Edward|King Edward]]''.{{Ref|name=KE|{{Cite Book|King Edward}}}}

===Undead===
Living Dragons can rarely become undead, as in the case of Durnehviir, a Dragon [[Lore:Necromancy|necromancer]] who became trapped in the Soul Cairn for so many centuries that his soul became bound to that plane, dooming him to an eternity of undeath.{{ref|name=DBDurnehviir|[[Skyrim:Durnehviir (dragon)|Durnehviir]]'s dialogue in ''[[SR:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} Even without a Dragon soul, the mortal remains of a Dragon can prove to be a dangerous opponent. [[Lore:Bone Dragon|Bone Dragon]]s are highly prized by necromancers for use as undead minions.{{ref|[[ON:Casting the Bones|Casting the Bones]] quest in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Although there have been no sightings of [[Lore:Vampirism|vampiric]] Dragons, [[Lore:Illusion|illusion]] [[Lore:Imp|imp]]s have been known to take on the form of small vampiric Dragons to scare away potential foes.{{ref|[[ON:Vampiric Dragon Imp|Vampiric Dragon Imp]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}

===Associated Creatures===
[[File:DF-creature-Dragonling.gif|A Dragonling|thumb|right]]
[[Lore:Wyrm|Wyrms]] are ethereal, elemental beings with Draconic appearances that are often summoned by Dragons.{{ref|name=ESOStormWyrm|[[ON:Storm Wyrm|Storm Wyrm]]s in [[ON:Online|ESO]]}} Dragons themselves are often referred to as wyrms. [[Lore:Wyvern|Wyverns]] are fire-breathing creatures of doubtful existence.{{ref|name=Alchemy}} The spell "Wyvern's Sting" is named after them.{{ref|[[Arena:The Known Spellbook|Wyvern's Sting]] spell in ''[[Arena:Arena|Arena]]''}} According to a fib from Alchemy, a member of the [[Lore:House of Reveries|House of Reveries]], those born to a Dragon and a mortal can turn into a wyvern during a full [[Lore:Moons|moon]].{{ref|name=Alchemy|[[ON:Alchemy (person)|Alchemy]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[ON:Summerset (Chapter)|Summerset]]''}} Due to the joking nature of her statement, this description of wyverns is highly unlikely. [[Lore:Lizard Man|Lizardmen]] have similarly been described as "a hybrid of a man and a dragon".{{ref|group=UOL|[[Arena:Unused Content#Monster Description|Unused Arena monster descriptions]]}} 

So-called "[[Lore:Dragonling|Dragonlings]]" (also called "Fairy Dragons"){{Ref|name=FDS|[[Daggerfall:Fairy dragon's scales|Fairy dragon's scales]] ingredient in ''[[DF:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}}{{Ref|group=UOL|name=DFTextures|Texture file names for [[DF:Dragonling|Dragonlings]] in ''[[DF:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}}  found around the [[Lore:Iliac Bay|Iliac Bay]] area are sometimes believed to be young Dragons,{{Ref|[[Daggerfall:The Dragonslayer|The Dragonslayer]] quest in ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}}{{ref|name=HistpryDF|''[[Daggerfall:Background History|Player Background History]]'' in ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}} however [[Lore:Fourth Era|Fourth Era]] scholars claim they are merely oversized [[Lore:Lizard|lizards]], with no relation to true Dragons.{{ref|name=TBD}} Despite this, Dragonlings appear quite intelligent: they can cast spells, speak Dragonish, and are considered very wise.{{ref|name=DUG}} Tiny Dragons have been seen in the [[Lore:Shivering Isles|Shivering Isles]], but given the nature of the Isles it is unclear if these are real Dragons.{{ref|[[Legends:Tiny Dragon|Tiny Dragon]] card in ''[[Legends:Legends|Legends]]''}} 

[[Lore:Dragon Frog|Dragon Frogs]] are fire-breathing winged [[Lore:Frog|frogs]] who stories in [[Lore:Hammerfell|Hammerfell]] claim to have once been actual Dragons before being transformed.{{ref|name=ONKindlespit|[[Online:Kindlespit Dragon Frog|Kindlespit Dragon Frog]] pet description in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} An alternative myth claims them to have been frogs who became more like Dragons.{{ref|name=ESOViri|[[Online:Viridescent Dragon Frog|Viridescent Dragon Frog]] pet description in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} [[Lore:Wamasu|Wamasu]] are large reptiles native to Black Marsh that have been mistaken for Dragons,{{ref|name=FAOT}} being colloquially known as "Swamp Dragons".{{Ref|name=TIEGtTBM|{{Cite Book|The Improved Emperor's Guide to Tamriel/Black Marsh}}}} Their eggs are sometimes mistaken for supposed Dragon eggs,{{ref|name=LADitSE}} the same being true for [[Lore:Sep Adder|sep adder]] eggs.{{ref|name=Almost|{{Cite Book|The Elf, the Egg, and the Almost-Dragon}}}} [[Lore:Sea-Drake|Sea-Drakes]] are large aquatic reptiles also seemingly named for Dragons.{{Ref|name=TIC|{{Cite Book|The Infernal City|ns_base=Books}}}}

===Draconic Imitations===
[[File:ON-crown store-Pyrodraconic Camel-Lizard.jpg|A Pyrodraconic Camel-Lizard, a poor attempt at recreating a Dragon magically|thumb|right]]
[[Lore:The Dragon|The Dragon]], one of the [[Lore:Luminary|Luminaries of Magic]], immortal beings of pure magic capable of choosing their own shapes, took the form of a female Dragon, having chosen the shape for its majesty.{{ref|name=Crow|[[Online:The Crow|The Crow]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{Ref|name=OND|[[Online:The Dragon|The Dragon]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} [[Lore:Peryite|Peryite]] also takes the form of a Dragon, but this may only be as some primordial jest to Akatosh.{{ref|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|Imperial Census of Daedra Lords|ns_base=GEN}}}} [[Lore:Daedric Titan|Daedric Titan]]s are a form of [[Lore:Daedra|Daedra]] that were first created by [[Lore:Molag Bal|Molag Bal]] in imitation of the Dragons. Molag Bal fashioned the first Daedric Titan from the skeleton of the Dragon [[Lore:Boziikkodstrun|Boziikkodstrun]].{{ref|name=DDTT|{{Cite Book|Daedra Dossier: The Titans}}}}

In {{Year|2E 582}}, the significance of a number of Dragons that followed Kaalgrontiid allowed them to be documented within the [[Lore:Infinite Archive|Infinite Archive]] in [[Lore:Apocrypha|Apocrypha]]. There, copies of various entities were subsequently created as [[Lore:Maligraphy|maligraphies]], creatures composed of vivified ink manifested by stories from books, serving as mindless extensions of the [[Lore:Daedric Lord|Daedric Lord]] [[Lore:Tho'at Replicanum|Tho'at Replicanum]]. Maligraphic copies of the Dragons Mulaamnir, Laatvulon, and Yolnahkriin were formed, and were confronted by an adventurer or two who were aided by augmentations directly from [[Lore:Hermaeus Mora|Hermaeus Mora]]. In addition, Tho'at Replicanum replicated herself throughout the Archive, with the form of a Glass Dragon being one of the shapes her copies took.{{ref|name=LAIA|{{Cite Book|Loremaster's Archive - Infinite Archive}}}}{{ref|name=MM|[[ON:Master Malkhest|Master Malkhest]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Necrom (Chapter)|Necrom]]''}}{{Ref|name=Enemies| [[ON:Infinite Archive|Dragon enemies]] in the [[ON:Infinite Archive|Infinite Archive]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} During that same year, a number of Daedra in the form of Glass Dragons were observed flying around the prison of the [[Lore:Daedric Prince|Daedric Prince]] [[Lore:Ithelia|Ithelia]], the Prince who Tho'at Replicanum is associated with.{{ref|group=UOL|1=[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=JhQeU-Izx1w Youtube Stream of ESO's ''10-Year Anniversary Celebration Livestream''], time stamp 38:53-39:36}}{{ref|name=ESOPrisoner|[[ON:Prisoner of Fate|Prisoner of Fate]] quest in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}

Some illusion imps use magic to disguise themselves as small Dragons, as a way to trick others into taking care of them. These disguised imps are sometimes known as "Dragon imps" and are often mistaken for baby Dragons.{{ref|name=BDI|[[Online:Blue Dragon Imp|Blue Dragon Imp]] pet description in [[ESO:ESO|ESO]]}} Followers of Akatosh sometimes create illusions of small, fiery Dragons to follow them.{{ref|name=SfDI|[[Online:Soulfire Dragon Illusion|Soulfire Dragon Illusion]] pet description in [[ESO:ESO|ESO]]}} Necromancers have been able to create skeletal [[Lore:Golem|constructs]] out of [[Lore:Bird|bird]] and [[Lore:Reptile|reptile]] bones that resemble miniature Bone Dragons.{{ref|[[Online:Small Bone Dragon Construct|Small Bone Dragon Construct]] pet description in [[ON:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|[[Online:Unholy Glow Bone Dragon|Unholy Glow Bone Dragon]] pet description in [[ON:Online|ESO]]}} The [[Lore:Telvanni|Telvanni]] magister [[Lore:Varkenel|Varkenel]] was once commissioned to create a Dragon. To approximate one, he used a mix of Telvanni and [[Lore:Wood Elf|Wood Elf]] techniques to create a fire-breathing [[Lore:Camel-Lizard|camel-lizard]] with red scales.{{ref|[[ON:Pyrodraconic Camel-Lizard|Pyrodraconic Camel-Lizard]] mount description in [[ESO:ESO|ESO]]}} Later he would create a product line of creatures known as the [[Lore:Scaleborn|Scaleborn]], this time with authentic draconic materials scavenged from Elsweyr.{{Ref|name=SS-R|[[ON:Scaleborn Senche-raht|Scaleborn Senche-raht]] mount description in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}

[[Lore:Tonal Dragon|Tonal Dragon]]s are ethereal beings resembling ghostly Dragons. They are created through [[Lore:Tonal Architecture|tonal architecture]].{{ref|[[Castles:Dragon|Tonal Dragon]]s in ''[[Castles:Castles|Castles]]''}} Clockwork Dragons are [[Lore:Factotum|constructs]] created by [[Lore:Sotha Sil|Sotha Sil]],{{Ref|name=LCD|[[Legends:Clockwork Dragon|Clockwork Dragon]] in ''[[Legends:Legends|Legends]]''}} though their exact origins are unknown.{{Ref|name=UOL|group=UOL}} They should not be confused with Clockwork Titans,{{Ref|name=Saint Olms|[[ON:Saint Olms the Just|Saint Olms the Just]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} as apart from some shared design elements found in Sotha Sil's creations, there is no other known connection between them.{{Ref|name=UOL|group=UOL|[[General:Pete Hines Legends Interview|Pete Hines Legends Interview]]}}

