==Uses==
[[File:SR-icon-weapon-Dragonbone Crossbow.png|thumb|left|A Dragonbone Crossbow]]
[[File:ON-concept-Dragonbone Style.jpg|Dragonbone Equipment|thumb|right]][[File:ON-crown store-Dragonscale Barded Senche.jpg|A Dragonscale Barded Senche|thumb|right]]
Dragonscale and Dragonbone have seen use in the creation of arms and armor since the Merethic Era.{{ref|[[Blades:Gauntlets of the Companions|Gauntlets of the Companions]] item description in ''[[Blades:Blades|Blades]]''}} There is considerable evidence that orthodox Dragon Priests had their armor crafted from genuine remains of the great creatures.{{ref|name=CM59|{{Cite Book|Crafting Motif 59: Scalecaller Style}}}} Some Dragons have awarded pieces of themselves willingly as part of an alliance or bargain. The Dragon [[Lore:Numinex|Numinex]] provided Draconic armor in exchange for his life.{{ref|name=Dov-rha Sabatons|[[ON:Dov-rha Sabatons|Dov-rha Sabatons]]'s antiquity codex entries in [[ON:Online|ESO]]}}

The practice of creating armor from Dragonscale was a common practice in Akaviri culture, and would become common in Imperial culture following their invasion in the First Era.{{ref|name=PGE1Cyro}} Members of the Dragonguard were also known to fashion armor from the bones of the Dragons they slew.{{ref|name=Bjor}} Imperial Dragonscale armor would still see use into the Third Era, after the majority of Dragons had died off or gone into hiding,{{ref|[[Morrowind:Imperial Dragonscale Armor|Imperial Dragonscale Armor]] in ''[[Morrowind:Morrowind|Morrowind]]''}} and the Imperial Legion was known to be in possession of stockpiles of Dragonbone well into the Fourth Era.{{ref|name=Bjor|{{Cite Book|ns_base=Skyrim|Bjormund's Diary}}}} Dragoneye helmets were known to exist in the late Third Era.{{ref|Dragoneye Helmets being present in [[Stormhold:Armor#Dragoneye Helmet|Stormhold]] and [[Dawnstar:Armor#Dragoneye Helmet|Dawnstar]]}} 

Dragonscale and Dragonbone were known to have become very rare materials as early as the Second Era,{{ref|name=CM59}} with them remaining that way into the early Fourth Era.{{ref|[[Blades:Dragon|Dragon]] item descriptions in ''[[Blades:Blades|Blades]]''}} Despite their rarity, they still saw occasional use in mundane life during this time. Various trinkets in the Second Era were known to be crafted out of the materials.{{ref|[[ON:Treasures D#Dragon-Scale Kitchen Knife|Dragon-Scale Kitchen Knife]] and [[ON:Treasures D#Dragonscale Purse|Dragonscale Purse]] item descriptions in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|[[ON:Treasures D#Dragonbone Comb|Dragonbone Comb]] and [[ON:Treasures D#Dragonbone Fang Caps|Dragonbone Fang Caps]] item descriptions in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Certain amulets of [[Lore:Talos|Talos]] are crafted with Dragonbone and scales.{{ref|{{Cite Book|The Crimson Dirks, v2}}}} The materials became easier to obtain after the return of the Dragons circa {{Year|4E 201}}.{{ref|[[Skyrim:Dragon Items|Dragon Items]] in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}

[[Lore:Alchemy D#Dragon's scales|Dragon's scales]],{{ref|[[Daggerfall:Dragon's scales|Dragon's scales]] in ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}} as well as their [[Lore:Alchemy D#Dragon Claw|claws]],{{ref|[[Blades:Dragon Claw|Dragon Claw]]s in ''[[Blades:Blades|Blades]]''}} [[Lore:Alchemy D#Dragon's Blood|blood]], and [[Lore:Alchemy D#Dragon's Bile|bile]], all have [[Lore:Alchemy|alchemical]] applications.{{ref|[[Online:Dragon's Blood|Dragon's Blood]] and [[Online:Dragon's Bile|Dragon's Bile]] in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Imbibing a Dragon's blood can grant the drinker increased power, and strengthen their talent in the use of the thu'um, but it is a brief benefit, as the blood also causes the body to start burning from the inside, dooming the drinker to a slow death.{{ref|name=Renald|[[Online:Chevalier Renald|Chevalier Renald]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=Grundwulf|[[Online:Grundwulf|Grundwulf]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=Sahrotnax|[[Online:Sahrotnax|Sahrotnax]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} Dragons are known to be vulnerable to weapons tipped with their own Dragonfire,{{ref|name=Dreek|[[Redguard:Dreekius|Dreekius]]' dialogue in ''[[Redguard:Redguard|Redguard]]''}} and [[Lore:Dragon Knights|Dragon Knights]] were known to ride upon large flaming [[Lore:Wolf|wolves]], which some speculated had been imbued with Dragonfire.{{Ref|name=Dragonfire Wolf|[[ON:Dragonfire Wolf|Dragonfire Wolf]] mount description in [[ON:Online|ESO]]}}

Roasted Dragon meat is said to be dense and thick with ligaments, and to have a taste similar to [[Lore:Chicken|fowl]].{{ref|{{Cite Book|Caluurion's Notes}}}}
