==Notes==
*{{LNote|nb1|1.|''The Wandering Spirits'' recounts the tale of Akha, who fathered offspring with the Winged Serpent, Mother Mammoth, and Dune Queen. Upon Akha's vanishing in the South, Alkosh appeared in his place. Alkosh took over the role and crown of the First Cat, "was granted rule over the myriad kingdoms of Akha along the Many Paths", and would watch over Akha's children. However, they rebelled against Alkosh, only for Khenarthi to fly across the Paths and restore him afterward. Together, they now oversee them.{{Ref|name=TWS}} The term "wayward children of Alkosh" was used by Clan Mother Tadali, a leader of a temple dedicated to Khenarthi, to describe Dragons.{{Ref|name=Tadali|[[ON:Clan Mother Tadali|Clan Mother Tadali]]'s dialogue in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Dragonhold|Dragonhold]]''}} Moreover, the Dragon [[Lore:Nahfahlaar|Nahfahlaar]] referred to Alkosh as his father.{{Ref|name=Nahfahlaar}}}}
*{{LNote|nb2|2.|An early idea for ''Skyrim'' would have had Jills as a group of Black Dragons serving Alduin.{{Ref|group=UOL|name=SRJills|Jill mention in the [https://www.vg247.com/dragonborn-again-bethesda-shows-skyrim-in-utah Dragonborn again: Bethesda shows Skyrim in Utah] article}}}}
*The use of "Dragon" in the nomenclature of northern Hammerfell is very common. From the smallest to the largest scale, there is the village of Dragon Gate,{{Ref|name=ARGate|[[Arena:Dragon Gate|Dragon Gate]] in ''[[Arena:Arena|Arena]]''}} the cities of [[Lore:Dragonstar|Dragonstar]]{{Ref|name=SKMap|[[:File:Shadowkey Map.jpg|Map of High Rock, Hammerfell, Skyrim Border – The Elder Scrolls Travels: Shadowkey]]}} and [[Lore:Dragontail|Dragontail]],{{Ref|name=DFDragontail|[[Daggerfall:Dragontail Mountains|Dragontail Mountains]] in ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}} the region known as [[Lore:Dragon Fields|Dragon Fields]],{{Ref|name=SKMap}} and the mountain ranges known as [[Lore:Dragontail Mountains|Dragontail]]{{Ref|name=DFDragontail}} and [[Lore:Dragon's Teeth Mountains|Dragon's Teeth]].{{Ref|name=AP|{{Cite Book|Arkngthamz-Phng (book)}}}}
*In the [[Lore:Fourth Era|Fourth Era]], there was some form of dance known as "Baby Drake".{{ref|[[Blades:Emotes#Baby Drake|Baby Drake]] emote in ''[[Blades:Blades|Blades]]''}}
*In the [[Morrowind Mod:Developer Mods|Developer Mod]] ''[[Morrowind Mod:Morrowind Advanced|Morrowind Advanced]]'' created by [[General:Gary Noonan|Gary Noonan]], there are several Draconic enemy creatures, such as the four-legged "[[:File:MWMOD-mod-RedWarriorDragon.jpg|Red Warrior Dragon]]", as well as the "[[:File:MWMOD-MWA-creature-Dragonian.jpeg|Dragonian]]" and "[[:File:MWMOD-MWA-creature-Wyvern.jpeg|Wyvern]]" represented by recolored existing enemies.

